elta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 43}, {"sha": "148566c9a50e27b695be7532a4e9a6cdc2094a2c", "short_sha": "148566c9a5", "subject": "Retract the superseded free-half claim WHERE IT LIVES, in FiberBound's own docstring", "summary": "**Correcting my own r4 text in place.** `FiberBound.lean` still said `baseChange_binders_stable` \"is the whole of the free half\" of extension-uniformity. It is not: class stability says nothing until an OBJECT carries the base-changed instances in the consumer`s spelling, and that lemma never mentions $C_\\kappa$, so it witnesses no re-firing. Marked SUPERSEDED in the section docstring and on the declaration, pointing at `ExtensionUniformity.vanishing_baseChangeField`.\n\n**Also flags the open-half mis-pricing at its source:** the paragraph blaming a non-transportable $n_0(\\kappa)$ is wrong in the same file`s own terms, since the threshold is existential and monotone in $b$. A reader who stops at `FiberBound` would otherwise inherit both errors.\n\n**Docstring-only:** every declaration line is byte-identical to HEAD (verified by diffing all signature/`variable`/`import`/`namespace` lines); the only apparent difference was a prose line beginning with the word \"theorem\" inside the replaced docstring. Kernel build 8691 exit 0, both modules rebuilt.", "created_at": "2026-07-29T04:34:38+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/FiberBound.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 22, "del": 4, "loc_before": 289, "loc_after": 307, "loc_code_before": 117, "loc_code_after": 117, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"theorem": 8}, "decl_after": {"theorem": 8}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}], "lean": {"files": 1, "add": 22, "del": 4, "loc_after": 307, "loc_code_after": 117, "loc_delta": 18, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {"theorem": 8}, "decl_delta": {}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 0}, {"sha": "b0fbfa1bfc323e310c20f60b92d0441a220b16fa", "short_sha": "b0fbfa1bfc", "subject": "Locate the real deliverable for genus invariance: AJC owns both sides of the comparison, not the comparison", "summary": "**Measured, not assumed.** With the carriers `rfl`-equal there is an AJC-native route besides porting AJCR wholesale, and every brick of it is present at HEAD: `Adelic.LaurentChartData.pullbackSquare` builds a 2-affine cover on `C` from any finite $\\pi$ (supplied by `MapToP1`), `Scheme.AffineCoverMVSquare.baseChangeField` transports it to $C_\\kappa$, and `h1_unit_baseChangeField_eq_genus` already reads $h^1(\\mathcal O_{C_\\kappa})$ on that transported cover AS $\\mathrm{genus}\\,C_\\kappa$.\n\n**So the residue is one specific equivalence,** not a chapter: the termwise base-change comparison $\\Gamma(C,V) \\otimes_k \\kappa \\simeq \\Gamma(C_\\kappa, V_\\kappa)$ on chart sections -- AJCR `relSectionsBaseChange`. AJC has both SIDES expressed on transported covers and lacks the map that makes them agree. That is the deliverable on either route.\n\n**A second carrier boundary the rfl does NOT cover:** AJCR states its genus invariance over `AffineTwoCover`, AJC over `AffineCoverMVSquare`, and `AffineTwoCover` occurs nowhere in AJC. Object-level defeq of the base-changed curve says nothing about the cover carriers, so a port crosses two boundaries, not one.", "created_at": "2026-07-29T04:19:39+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/ExtensionUniformity.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 21, "del": 0, "loc_before": 327, "loc_after": 348, "loc_code_before": 100, "loc_code_after": 100, "sorry_befo